# Architecture

```
app/                 routes, layout, globals.css
components/          chrome (nav, theme, reveal, scroll)
components/hero/     hero + 3D + pointer/magnetic motion
components/sections/ About, Skills, Projects, Contact, Footer
lib/data.ts          all static content
public/              served assets (use this, not assets/)
legacy/              unused vanilla site — leave alone
```

## Placement

- New page sections → `components/sections/`, then compose in `app/page.tsx`.
- Hero-only UI → `components/hero/`. Do not dump hero widgets into `sections/`.
- Shared chrome → `components/` root (`Navbar`, `ThemeToggle`, `Reveal`).
- Copy, links, projects, skills → `lib/data.ts`, not hardcoded in JSX.
- Images → `public/`. `assets/` is a duplicate; do not add new files there.

## Patterns already in use

- One home route (`/`). Sections use hash ids (`#about`, `#skills`, …).
- Client islands: `'use client'` only where motion, 3D, or browser APIs need it.
- Dynamic 3D: `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` (see `HeroRight.tsx` / `HeroImage.tsx`).
- Pointer field shared via `components/hero/pointer.tsx`.
- GSAP intro + ScrollTrigger live in `heroAnimations.ts` and `SmoothScroll.tsx`.
